diff --git a/features/editing-todos.feature b/features/editing-todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e4f1fec
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/editing-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@
+Feature: Editing Todos
+  As a user
+  I want to edit existing todo titles
+  So that I can correct or update my task descriptions
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is open
+
+  Rule: Activating edit mode
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a todo label enters edit mode
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the label of "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo item should have the editing class
+    And the edit input should contain "Buy milk"
+    And the edit input should be focused
+
+  Rule: Saving an edit
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit by pressing Enter
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the label of "Buy milk" to edit it
+    And I change the value to "Buy oat milk"
+    And I press Enter
+    Then the todo should display "Buy oat milk"
+    And the editing class should be removed
+
+  Scenario: Saving an edit on blur
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the label of "Buy milk" to edit it
+    And I change the value to "Buy oat milk"
+    And I blur the edit input
+    Then the todo should display "Buy oat milk"
+    And the editing class should be removed
+
+  Rule: Discarding an edit
+
+  Scenario: Pressing Escape discards changes
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the label of "Buy milk" to edit it
+    And I change the value to "Buy oat milk"
+    And I press Escape
+    Then the todo should display "Buy milk"
+    And the editing class should be removed
+
+  Rule: Empty title destroys the todo
+
+  Scenario: Clearing the title and saving destroys the todo
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the label of "Buy milk" to edit it
+    And I change the value to ""
+    And I press Enter
+    Then the todo list should not contain "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Title trimmed to empty destroys the todo
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the label of "Buy milk" to edit it
+    And I change the value to "   "
+    And I press Enter
+    Then the todo list should not contain "Buy milk"
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/features/managing-todos.feature b/features/managing-todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..aea0d7a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/managing-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,104 @@
+Feature: Managing Todos
+  As a user
+  I want to add, complete, and clear todos
+  So that I can track what I need to do
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is open
+
+  Rule: Empty state
+
+  Scenario: The main section and footer are hidden when there are no todos
+    Given the app has no todos
+    Then the main section should not be visible
+    And the footer should not be visible
+
+  Rule: Adding a new todo
+
+  Scenario: Creating a todo by pressing Enter
+    Given the input field is focused
+    When I type "Buy milk" into the new-todo input
+    And I press Enter
+    Then a new todo "Buy milk" appears in the list
+    And the new-todo input is cleared
+
+  Scenario: Trimming whitespace from a new todo
+    Given the input field is focused
+    When I type "   Write code   " into the new-todo input
+    And I press Enter
+    Then a new todo "Write code" appears in the list
+
+  Scenario: Ignoring empty input
+    Given the input field is focused
+    When I press Enter with an empty input
+    Then no new todo is added to the list
+
+  Rule: Completing a todo
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a single todo as completed
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When I click the toggle checkbox on "Buy milk"
+    Then "Buy milk" should be marked as completed
+
+  Scenario: Unchecking a completed todo
+    Given the todo list contains a completed todo "Buy milk"
+    When I click the toggle checkbox on "Buy milk"
+    Then "Buy milk" should be marked as active
+
+  Rule: Mark all as complete
+
+  Scenario: Toggling all todos as completed
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Write code"
+    When I click the "Mark all as complete" toggle
+    Then all todos should be marked as completed
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all checkbox state reflects individual completions
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Write code"
+    And I mark "Buy milk" as completed
+    And I mark "Write code" as completed
+    Then the "Mark all as complete" checkbox should be checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all clears when not all todos are completed
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Write code"
+    And I mark "Buy milk" as completed
+    Then the "Mark all as complete" checkbox should not be checked
+
+  Scenario: Clearing the "Mark all as complete" state via "Clear completed"
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Write code"
+    And all todos are marked as completed
+    When I click "Clear completed"
+    Then the "Mark all as complete" checkbox should not be checked
+
+  Rule: Item counter
+
+  Scenario: Displaying the count of active todos
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Write code"
+    When I mark "Buy milk" as completed
+    Then the todo count should show "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Pluralizing the item counter
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Write code"
+    Then the todo count should show "2 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows zero items when all are completed
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When I mark "Buy milk" as completed
+    Then the todo count should show "0 items left"
+
+  Rule: Clearing completed todos
+
+  Scenario: Removing completed todos via "Clear completed"
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Write code"
+    And I mark "Buy milk" as completed
+    When I click "Clear completed"
+    Then the todo list should contain "Write code"
+    And the todo list should not contain "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Hiding "Clear completed" when no todos are completed
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    Then the "Clear completed" button should not be visible
+
+  Scenario: Showing "Clear completed" when there are completed todos
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When I mark "Buy milk" as completed
+    Then the "Clear completed" button should be visible
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7a67f51
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+Feature: Persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to persist across page reloads
+  So that I do not lose my task list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is open
+
+  Rule: Saving to localStorage
+
+  Scenario: Todos are saved to localStorage on creation
+    Given the app has no todos
+    When I type "Buy milk" into the new-todo input
+    And I press Enter
+    Then the todos in localStorage should contain "Buy milk"
+    And the localStorage key should be prefixed with "todos-"
+
+  Scenario: Completed state is persisted
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When I mark "Buy milk" as completed
+    Then localStorage should record "Buy milk" as completed
+
+  Scenario: Edited title is persisted
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk"
+    When I change the title of "Buy milk" to "Buy oat milk"
+    Then the todos in localStorage should contain "Buy oat milk"
+    And the todos in localStorage should not contain "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Cleared todos are removed from localStorage
+    Given the todo list contains "Buy milk" and "Write code"
+    When I mark "Buy milk" as completed
+    And I click "Clear completed"
+    Then localStorage should contain "Write code"
+    And localStorage should not contain "Buy milk"
+
+  Rule: Loading from localStorage
+
+  Scenario: Todos are restored from localStorage on page load
+    Given localStorage contains an active todo "Buy milk"
+    When I reload the app
+    Then the todo list should contain "Buy milk"
+
+  Scenario: Completed state is restored from localStorage
+    Given localStorage contains a completed todo "Buy milk"
+    When I reload the app
+    Then "Buy milk" should be marked as completed
+
+  Scenario: Multiple todos are restored from localStorage
+    Given localStorage contains todos "Buy milk" and "Write code"
+    When I reload the app
+    Then the todo list should show 2 items
+
+  Scenario: Empty localStorage means no todos
+    Given localStorage has no todos
+    When I reload the app
+    Then the main section should not be visible
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/features/routing.feature b/features/routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..fb3a67f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+Feature: Routing and Filtering
+  As a user
+  I want to filter the todo list by completion state
+  So that I can focus on active or completed items
+
+  Background:
+    Given the TodoMVC app is open
+    And the todo list contains "Buy milk", "Write code", and "Pay bills"
+    And I mark "Write code" as completed
+
+  Rule: Default route
+
+  Scenario: The default route shows all todos
+    Given the app is at the default route
+    Then the todo list should show 3 items
+    And the "All" filter link should have the selected class
+
+  Rule: Active filter
+
+  Scenario: The active route shows only active todos
+    When I navigate to the "#/active" route
+    Then the todo list should show 2 items
+    And the displayed items should be "Buy milk" and "Pay bills"
+    And the "Active" filter link should have the selected class
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo while on the active filter hides it
+    Given I am on the "#/active" route
+    When I mark "Buy milk" as completed
+    Then the todo list should show 1 item
+    And the displayed items should be "Pay bills"
+
+  Rule: Completed filter
+
+  Scenario: The completed route shows only completed todos
+    When I navigate to the "#/completed" route
+    Then the todo list should show 1 item
+    And the displayed item should be "Write code"
+    And the "Completed" filter link should have the selected class
+
+  Scenario: Unchecking a todo while on the completed filter hides it
+    Given I am on the "#/completed" route
+    When I mark "Write code" as active
+    Then the todo list should show 0 items
+
+  Rule: Filter links
+
+  Scenario: Clicking a filter link changes the active filter
+    Given the app is at the default route
+    When I click the "Active" filter link
+    Then the URL hash should be "#/active"
+    And the "Active" filter link should have the selected class
+
+  Scenario: The active filter persists on reload
+    Given I navigate to the "#/active" route
+    When I reload the app
+    Then the "Active" filter link should have the selected class
+    And the todo list should show only active items
\ No newline at end of file
